From ab22f3d5bba07e145111aaf87b7752c9ee8b5b47 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 02:46:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] system: the help of the diagnostics says what the boot menu
 does while they are on

While the switch of the diagnostics is on, the boot menus now start the
kernel with initcall_debug=1 (hades-diag, kernel-line.sh): the journal
then has a line for each driver that the kernel starts and one when it
returns, so that the journal of a start that stops while drivers start,
which the next start saves, names the driver that never returned. That
changes a line of the boot menus, which nothing on the screen said: the
help shown when the diagnostics are turned on says it now, in plain
words, in English and in the three Spanish translations.
---
 resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po | 2 +-
 resources/language/resource.language.es_ar/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_es/strings.po | 4 ++--
 resources/language/resource.language.es_mx/strings.po | 4 ++--
 4 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
index 0800c9b..627e0d1 100644
--- a/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/resources/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1597,7 +1597,7 @@ msgid "Changing the switch of the diagnostics..."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33633"
-msgid "The diagnostics are on from the next start of this system.[CR][CR]What they save at each start: the graphics and the displays, the logs of Kodi and of the system, how the system was turned off, and what is sent to the TV around each Dolby Vision video.[CR][CR]Where: in the folder hades-diag of the boot partition, which Windows shows as the drive LIBREELEC on a USB drive. The last eight starts are kept, usually 1 to 5 MB each, and nothing is written while that partition has less than 128 MB free. The journal of each start is kept in the storage for the next one, 16 MB at most.[CR][CR]Every file goes through the filter of the diagnostics first: the addresses, serial numbers and the names of your networks, drives, films and of this system become markers, and keys and passwords are taken out. Nothing is sent anywhere.[CR][CR]To take what they saved: \"Create a diagnostic report\", or \"Copy the diagnostics to a USB drive\". Turned off, nothing more is saved, and what was saved stays. It is the same switch as the box \"Save diagnostics there\" of the installer for Windows: the file DIAG-ON.TXT on that partition."
+msgid "The diagnostics are on from the next start of this system.[CR][CR]What they save at each start: the graphics and the displays, the logs of Kodi and of the system, how the system was turned off, and what is sent to the TV around each Dolby Vision video.[CR][CR]Where: in the folder hades-diag of the boot partition, which Windows shows as the drive LIBREELEC on a USB drive. The last eight starts are kept, usually 1 to 5 MB each, and nothing is written while that partition has less than 128 MB free. The journal of each start is kept in the storage for the next one, 16 MB at most. While they are on, the boot menu also has the system note each driver as it starts it, so that a start that stops says which driver it was waiting for.[CR][CR]Every file goes through the filter of the diagnostics first: the addresses, serial numbers and the names of your networks, drives, films and of this system become markers, and keys and passwords are taken out. Nothing is sent anywhere.[CR][CR]To take what they saved: \"Create a diagnostic report\", or \"Copy the diagnostics to a USB drive\". Turned off, nothing more is saved, and what was saved stays. It is the same switch as the box \"Save diagnostics there\" of the installer for Windows: the file DIAG-ON.TXT on that partition."
 msgstr ""
 
 msgctxt "#33634"
